{"id":"word:hebrew:H205","type":"word","title":"אָוֶן","subtitle":"H205 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"strictly nothingness ; also trouble , vanity , wickedness ; specifically an idol","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אָוֶן (H205) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 79 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אָוֶן (ʼâven) means strictly nothingness ; also trouble , vanity , wickedness ; specifically an idol First listed occurrence: 1Sam 15 23."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אָוֶן","transliteration":"ʼâven","pronunciation":"aw-ven'","strong":"H205","lemmaId":"hebrew:H205","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["אָ֑וֶן","אָֽוֶן","אָ֥וֶן","אָ֨וֶן֙","אָ֔וֶן"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",66],["HC/Ncmsa",4],["HR/Ncmsa",3],["HNcmpa",2],["HNcmsc/Sp2fs",1],["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",1],["HNcmsc/Sp3mp",1],["HTd/Ncmsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"strictly nothingness ; also trouble , vanity , wickedness ; specifically an idol","usage":"affliction, evil, false, idol, iniquity, mischief, mourners(-ing), naught, sorrow, unjust, unrighteous, vain, vanity, wicked(-ness). Compare 369 .","full":"H205. aven אָ֫וֶן 85 noun masculine Job 5:6 trouble, sorrow, wickedness — absolute Num 23:21 +; suffix אוֺנִי Gen 35:18 etc.; plural אוֺנִים Hosea 9:4 — 1 trouble, sorrow בֶּןאֿוֺנִי son of my trouble or sorrow Gen 35:18 (E); בְּיַעֲקֹב אָוֶן הִבִּיט לֹא Num 23:21 (song of Balaam), he doth not behold trouble in Jacob (|| he doth not see misery — עָמָל — in Isr); often || עָמָל Psa 7:15 ( יְחַבֶּלאָֿוֶן הִנֵּה lo he travaileth with trouble || שָׁ֑קֶר וְיָלַד עָמָל וְהָרָה , yea he hath conceived misery & brought forth a lie ), probably thence Job 15:35 ( אָוֶן וְיָלֹד עָמָל הָרהֹ ) = Isa 59:4 ; compare וָאָוֶן עָמָל Psa 10:7 ; 55:11 ; 90:10 ; Job 4:8 ; 5:6 ; Isa 10:1 (see עָמָל ); also יִקְצָראָֿוֶן עַוְלָה זוֺרֵעַ Prov 22:8 the sower of iniquity shall reap trouble ; in this sense elsewhere only Deut 26:14 ; Prov 12:21 ; Jer 4:15 ; Hab 3:7 ; Amos 5:5 , plural intensive אוֺנִים לֶחֶם bread of trouble, sorrow, or mourning Hosea 9:4 . 2 idolatry Hosea 12:12 ; Isa 41:29 ; הַפְצַ֑ר וּתְרָפִים אָוֶן stubbornness is idolatry & (the use of) teraphim 1Sam 15:23 (poetry source); בֵּית אָוֶן Hosea 4:15 (for אֵל בֵּית because Bethel, house of God, is given over to idolatry) so also 5:8 ; 10:5 compare א ׳בָּמוֺת 10:8 ; א ׳בִּקְעַת Amos 1:5 (Baalbek); א ׳בַּחוּרֵי read אֹן אוֺן, = On, Heliopolis Ezek 30:17 ; &#8212; abstract for concrete = idols Isa 66:3 . 3 trouble of iniquity, wickedness , אָוֶן מְתֵי Job 22:15 ; א ׳אַנְשֵׁי 34:36 = men of trouble, troublers, wicked men ; compare א ׳אִישׁ Prov 6:12 ; Isaiah 55:17; אָוֶן מֹּעֲלֵי workers of trouble, evil-doers, workers of iniquity Job 31:3 ; 34:8 , 22 ; Psa 5:6 ; + (16 t. chiefly late Psalms) Prov 10:29 ; 21:15 ; Isa 31:2 ; Hosea 6:8 ; אָוֶן מַחְשְׁבוֺת thoughts of trouble, wicked imaginations Prov 6:18 ; Isa 59:7 ; Jer 4:14 ; often of words & thoughts Job 11:11 + (5 t.) Psa 36:5 + (9 t.) Prov 17:4 ; 19:28 ; 30:20 ; Isa 29:20 ; 32:6 ; 58:9 ; 59:6 ; Ezek 11:2 ; Micah 2:1 ; Hab 1:3 ; Zech 10:2 ; וַעֲצָרָה אָוֶן אוּכַל לֹא Isa 1:13 I cannot bear iniquity with the solemn meeting (RV & most modern; AV it is iniquity, even the solemn meeting ). אֹן sorrow , see אָוֶן .","rootNote":"from an unused root perhaps meaning properly, to pant (hence, to exert oneself, usually in vain; to come to naught );","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Sam 15 23","keyReferences":["1Sam 15 23","Amos 5 5","Deut 26 14","Ezek 11 2","Hab 1 3","Hab 3 7","Hos 6 8","Hos 9 4"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":79,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Sam 15 23","book":"1Sam","chapter":15,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/אָ֥וֶן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Amos 5 5","book":"Amos","chapt